@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: WWW Resource Library
	Frontend testing for the www resource library page

Scenario: Filter Resources By Type
	End users should be able to filter resources by type and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the url "/resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Type | Business Whitepapers |
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Study"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Type | Case Studies |
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Case Study"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Type | E-books |
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Study"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Type | Product Info |
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Study"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Type | Research Reports |
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Study"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Type | Technical Whitepapers |
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Study"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"

Scenario: Filter Resources By Solution
	End users should be able to filter resources by solution and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the url "/resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solution | Customer Portals |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of a Portal"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "What is a Portal?"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Portal Best Practices"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solution | Knowledge Management Platforms |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "New knowledge management platform for leading marketing research company"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of a Portal"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "What is a Portal?"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Portal Best Practices"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solution | E-commerce Websites |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "7 Best Practices for B2B E-Commerce Success"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "How to Use Your E-Commerce Site to Empower Your Sales Team"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "The B2B E-Commerce RFP Kit"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "B2BecNews Report - Choosing the Right E-Commerce Platform"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "New knowledge management platform for leading marketing research company"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solution | Public Websites |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Public website gives access to new mobile audience with"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "7 Best Practices for B2B E-Commerce Success"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "How to Use Your E-Commerce Site to Empower Your Sales Team"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The B2B E-Commerce RFP Kit"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "B2BecNews Report - Choosing the Right E-Commerce Platform"

Scenario: Filter Resources By Industry
	End users should be able to filter resources by industry and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the url "/resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Industry | Aerospace & Defense |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "100,000 users united through a self-service portal, simplifying incident management"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "The new customer portal, modern and accessible 24/7, simplifies the day-to-day life of 3,000 helicopter"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Industry | Healthcare |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Transforming the Healthcare Industry with Liferay DXP"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of the Portal in Healthcare"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Modern healthcare experience with a mobile-friendly new site"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "100,000 users united through a self-service portal, simplifying incident management"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The new customer portal, modern and accessible 24/7, simplifies the day-to-day life of 3,000 helicopter"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Industry | Government (Federal) |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Transforming the Digital Experience in Australian Government"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "A new intranet for the US Navy serves 40,000 users with exceptional performance and user satisfaction"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Digital Transformation in the UK Public Sector"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Council of Europe creates effective communication tool with Liferay Portal"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Transforming the Healthcare Industry with Liferay DXP"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of the Portal in Healthcare"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Modern healthcare experience with a mobile-friendly new site"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Industry | Media/Entertainment |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Media giant rolls out 70+ websites with new standardized solution"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Transforming the Digital Experience in Australian Government"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "A new intranet for the US Navy serves 40,000 users with exceptional performance and user satisfaction"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Digital Transformation in the UK Public Sector"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Council of Europe creates effective communication tool with Liferay Portal"

Scenario: Filter Resources By Topic
	End users should be able to filter resources by topic and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the url "/resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Topic | Customer Experience |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Leveraging AI to Improve the B2B Customer Experience"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Four Strategies to Transform Your Customer Experience"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Liferay DXP Business Overview: Customer Experience"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Three Key Strategies for Consistent Customer Experiences"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Topic | Digital Strategy |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Digital by Default, Open by Design"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "6 Essential Web Strategies for Financial Services"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Leveraging AI to Improve the B2B Customer Experience"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Four Strategies to Transform Your Customer Experience"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Liferay DXP Business Overview: Customer Experience"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Three Key Strategies for Consistent Customer Experiences"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Topic | Digital Transformation |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "IDC Infobrief: Accelerating Customer Experience Transformation in Insurance Through Digital Experience Platforms"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Jumpstart Your Digital Transformation With a Digital Experience Platform"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Building Trust in Government Through Digital Transformation"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Digital by Default, Open by Design"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "6 Essential Web Strategies for Financial Services"

Scenario: Filter Resources Using Multiple Criteria
	End users should be able to filter resources by multiple criteria and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the url "/resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solution      | Collaboration Platforms |
	| Industry      | Government (Federal)    |
	| Topic         | Digital Transformation  |
	| Resource Type | Case Studies            |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "New platform skyrockets search usage"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solution      | Customer Portals    |
	| Industry      | Aerospace & Defense |
	| Topic         | Customer Experience |
	| Resource Type | Case Studies        |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "The new customer portal, modern and accessible 24/7, simplifies the day-to-day life of 3,000 helicopter"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "New platform skyrockets search usage"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solution      | E-commerce Websites |
	| Industry      | Engineering         |
	| Topic         | All Topics          |
	| Resource Type | Research Reports    |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "The Relevance of Customer Centricity in Manufacturing"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The new customer portal, modern and accessible 24/7, simplifies the day-to-day life of 3,000 helicopter"
	When I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solution      | Public Websites        |
	| Industry      | Financial Services     |
	| Topic         | Digital Transformation |
	| Resource Type | Case Studies           |
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "modern approach to banking"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Integrated portal platform at center of Britam"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The Relevance of Customer Centricity in Manufacturing"